Q: Can you make transform:scale() account for margins? A: <p>Try with zoom instead</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>* {
  margin: 0;
}

div {
  width: 50px;
  height: 50px;
  background-color: red;
  margin-left: 50px;
  margin-bottom: 20px;
}

.scaleDiv {
  zoom: .2;
}</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class='scaleDiv'&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>
